10.1 PayFast

Integrate PayFast for South African online payments.

Requirements:

- Use the current official PayFast integration documentation.
- Support the payment flow and methods available to the merchant account.
- Implement server-side payment initiation.
- Generate the required signature using the official specification.
- Validate the payment notification and all applicable signature, source, amount, merchant and reference checks.
- Verify notifications with PayFast's official validation process where required.
- Support ITN/webhook processing.
- Verify the transaction independently when required.
- Handle successful, failed, cancelled and pending payments.
- Support refunds only through the actual documented API or approved merchant workflow.
- Store provider transaction IDs and audit events.
- Support sandbox testing.

Do not treat a browser redirect or success-page visit as proof of payment.

10.2 Payflex

Integrate Payflex as a buy-now-pay-later payment option where the merchant and customer are eligible.

Requirements:

- Consult the current official Payflex merchant and developer documentation.
- Confirm eligibility, available product types, supported currencies and settlement rules.
- Implement the actual supported checkout or hosted-payment flow.
- Handle approval, rejection, cancellation and pending states.
- Verify payment status through documented server-side mechanisms.
- Process signed callbacks or webhooks where supported.
- Prevent orders from being fulfilled before the required confirmation.
- Handle refunds and cancellations according to actual provider capabilities.
- Clearly display the terms supplied or approved by Payflex.

Do not promise that every customer will qualify for instalments.

Do not invent Payflex endpoints or assume that an API is available to every merchant. If direct integration requires merchant approval or a partner integration, document that dependency and complete the adapter only to the extent supported by official documentation.

