24. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

1. Do not deliver a static mockup in place of the application.
2. Do not create fake payment-success flows that can mark orders as paid.
3. Do not invent payment APIs, credentials, merchant permissions or gateway capabilities.
4. Do not expose secrets to the browser.
5. Do not trust browser-submitted prices or stock quantities.
6. Do not fulfil orders until the required payment confirmation is verified.
7. Do not oversell inventory through concurrent checkout requests.
8. Do not invent live sales data, testimonials, product specifications or delivery promises.
9. Do not silently omit requested features.
10. Do not replace real functionality with TODO comments without documenting the limitation.
11. Do not claim tests passed unless they were executed and passed.
12. Do not claim the site is production-ready until its security, payment, operational and legal launch requirements have been reviewed.
13. Prefer complete, maintainable implementations over unnecessary complexity.
14. If credentials or merchant approval are unavailable, finish all independently implementable code and clearly document the exact next steps.
15. Ask questions only when a missing decision genuinely blocks implementation. Otherwise use sensible, documented defaults.

